## 1. The pre-existing visualiser, measured

Files: inspector/index.html (2420 B), inspector.css (3574 B), inspector.js (9555 B),
served by `python main.py inspect` (the `inspector/` directory is untouched by
this work).

`python main.py inspect --cold-inspector --no-browser --port 8799` booted about
60 s and returned 4155 bytes of JSON:

  counts: {'nodes': 0, 'edges': 0, 'rules': 217, 'derivations': 0,
           'search_history': 0, 'search_comparisons': 0, 'search_jobs': 0}
  cytoscape elements: 15 nodes, 10 edges
  node kinds: ['rule_hyperedge', 'term']; edge kinds: ['rule_incidence_in', 'rule_incidence_out']

The graph pane can only show rule edges, because the packs load rules and no
carrier content. The cause is in MachineRuntime.cytoscape_view, which calls
M.EdgeInputs(edge) on every graph edge; a canonical hyperedge is a Pair. Repro
against the public API (fresh runtime, two nodes, one Pair hyperedge):

  $ python -u -  (add_node x2, add_edge(Pair(Linked, hub, spoke)), cytoscape_view())
  cytoscape_view raised: AttributeError: 'Pair' object has no attribute 'inputs'

Further gaps read off inspector.js: Cytoscape is loaded from https://unpkg.com,
every refresh calls cy.destroy() and rebuilds the whole graph, there is no
recording/timeline/replay, and the viewer boots its own runtime, so it shows a
copy rather than a running Machine.

